{1 = 1-9}
11.	@wPN{Nibruta-lu}, 
12.	the son of the merchant @wPN{Lugal-šuba}, 
13.	has had this tin axe made for @wDN{Nergal}. 
14.	Its wooden part is of @fsux{arganum} tree of the mountains, 
15.	a wood which is superior even to the @fsux{alal} stone; 
16.	its stone part is of @fsux{antasura}, 
17.	a stone which has no equal. 
18.	The arm of the man who strikes  
19.	with it will never get tired. 

{10 = 10-16}
1010.	Should it break, 
1011.	I will repair it for @wDN{Nergal}. 
1012.	Should it disappear, 
1013.	I will replace it for him. 
1014.	May @wDN{Nergal} look after me during my life, 
1015.	and may he provide me with clean  
1016.	water in the underworld after my death. 
